Bag of holding explosions should never happen, even if people make
typos.  This isn't like accidently eating a cockatrice corpse, where
mistyping a single letter can instantly kill you.  When you place
objects inside of a container, you get a special selection screen, and
the items don't go into the container until you leave this screen.
Therefore, even if you make a typo, and select a wand of cancellation
to go into a bag of holding -- as long as you double-check the
selection screen before leaving it, then you should be able to notice
your mistake before it causes the bag of holding to explode.

Wands of cancellation can be easily identified by using two charges of
the wand, and if you avoid putting wands of cancellation into a bag of
holding (or an unidentified bag), then you should be able to avoid
surprise wand-related bag of holding explosions.  And if you avoid
putting unidentified bags into a bag of holding (or an unidentified
bag), then you should be able to avoid surprise bag-related bag of
holding explosions.


